#!/bin/sh
# Drop number-up for jobs macOS has already imposed itself.
#
# macOS renders Layout > "Pages per Sheet" client-side in cgpdftopdf and then
# STILL forwards number-up in the IPP job ticket. pdftopdf, first filter in the
# chain here, takes that at face value and imposes a second time: a 28-page
# document asked for at 4-up arrived as a 7-page pre-imposed PDF and printed as
# 16 logical pages per sheet (4x4).
#
# The server is not at fault under RFC 8011 — number-up is a Job Template
# attribute and a conformant printer performs it. The job ticket is the thing
# that is self-contradictory: it declares PMTotalSidesImaged=7 and asks for
# number-up=4 in the same breath. Apple's bug (apple/cups#5361); upstream CUPS
# was offered this exact workaround as OpenPrinting/cups#971 and closed it
# wontfix/platform-issue, so it has to live here.
#
# Why not the obvious alternatives:
#   - number-up-default=1 cannot work. Printer defaults only fill in attributes
#     the client omitted, and this queue's default was ALREADY 1 when the 16-up
#     misprint happened.
#   - number-up-supported cannot be narrowed per-queue; it is a file-scope
#     constant in cupsd, and add_job() validates against a hardcoded list anyway.
#   - Nothing advertised can help: cgpdftopdf reads only APAirPrint, cupsFax,
#     cupsMaxCopies, DefaultOutputOrder and PageStackOrder from the PPD, and
#     takes number-up straight from the job options.
#
# Stripping is CONDITIONAL, keyed on macOS's own "I already imposed this" flag,
# so a non-Apple client that genuinely wants the server to do N-up still gets it.
# When the box is unticked macOS sends the token as
# "nocom.apple.print.PrintSettings.PMLayoutNUp..b.", which deliberately does not
# match the leading-space pattern below.
#
# Only pdftopdf needs wrapping: it is the sole imposer in the PDF chain. pstops
# is not a top-level filter here — pdftops spawns it as a DSC post-processor —
# and the shimmed chain was verified end to end (7 pages in, 7 pages out, with
# pstops confirmed not to re-arm).
real=/usr/lib/cups/filter/pdftopdf
opts=$5

case " $opts " in
  *" com.apple.print.PrintSettings.PMLayoutNUp..b. "*)
    opts=$(printf '%s' "$opts" | sed -E 's/(^| )number-up(-layout)?=[^ ]*//g')
    ;;
esac

# cupsd passes the file as $6 when it is not streaming on stdin; preserve both.
if [ "$#" -ge 6 ]; then
  exec "$real" "$1" "$2" "$3" "$4" "$opts" "$6"
fi
exec "$real" "$1" "$2" "$3" "$4" "$opts"
